BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* (4. When the code needs to remain compatible with older versions of Python that don't support the) Tj T* (feature recommended by the style guide.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Code Lay-out) Tj T* () Tj T* (Indentation) Tj T* () Tj T* (Use 4 spaces per indentation level.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Continuation lines should align wrapped elements either vertically using Python's implicit line) Tj T* (joining inside parentheses, brackets and braces, or using a *hanging indent* [#fn-hi]_.  When) Tj T* (using a hanging indent the following should be considered; there should be no arguments on the) Tj T* (first line and further indentation should be used to clearly distinguish itself as a) Tj T* (continuation line:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Aligned with opening delimiter.) Tj T* (foo = long_function_name\(var_one, var_two,) Tj T* (var_three, var_four\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Add 4 spaces \(an extra level of indentation\) to distinguish arguments from the rest.) Tj T* (def long_function_name\() Tj T* (var_one, var_two, var_three,) Tj T* (var_four\):) Tj T* (print\(var_one\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Hanging indents should add a level.) Tj T* (foo = long_function_name\() Tj T* (var_one, var_two,) Tj T* (var_three, var_four\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Arguments on first line forbidden when not using vertical alignment.) Tj T* (foo = long_function_name\(var_one, var_two,) Tj T* (var_three, var_four\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Further indentation required as indentation is not distinguishable.) Tj T* (def long_function_name\() Tj T* (var_one, var_two, var_three,) Tj T* (var_four\):) Tj T* (print\(var_one\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (The 4-space rule is optional for continuation lines.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Optional:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Hanging indents *may* be indented to other than 4 spaces.) Tj T* (foo = long_function_name\() Tj T* (var_one, var_two,) Tj T* (var_three, var_four\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 2 of 27) Tj T* ET
endstream
