BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (When the conditional part of an if-statement is long enough to require that it be written across) Tj T* (multiple lines, it's worth noting that the combination of a two character keyword \(i.e. if\),) Tj T* (plus a single space, plus an opening parenthesis creates a natural 4-space indent for the) Tj T* (subsequent lines of the multiline conditional.  This can produce a visual conflict with the) Tj T* (indented suite of code nested inside the if-statement, which would also naturally be indented to) Tj T* (4 spaces.  This PEP takes no explicit position on how \(or whether\) to further visually) Tj T* (distinguish such conditional lines from the nested suite inside the if-statement. Acceptable) Tj T* (options in this situation include, but are not limited to:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# No extra indentation.) Tj T* (if \(this_is_one_thing and) Tj T* (that_is_another_thing\):) Tj T* (do_something\(\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Add a comment, which will provide some distinction in editors) Tj T* (# supporting syntax highlighting.) Tj T* (if \(this_is_one_thing and) Tj T* (that_is_another_thing\):) Tj T* (# Since both conditions are true, we can frobnicate.) Tj T* (do_something\(\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Add some extra indentation on the conditional continuation line.) Tj T* (if \(this_is_one_thing) Tj T* (and that_is_another_thing\):) Tj T* (do_something\(\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (\(Also see the discussion of whether to break before or after binary operators below.\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (The closing brace/bracket/parenthesis on multiline constructs may either line up under the first) Tj T* (non-whitespace character of the last line of list, as in:) Tj T* () Tj T* (my_list = [) Tj T* (1, 2, 3,) Tj T* (4, 5, 6,) Tj T* (]) Tj T* (result = some_function_that_takes_arguments\() Tj T* ('a', 'b', 'c',) Tj T* ('d', 'e', 'f',) Tj T* (\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (or it may be lined up under the first character of the line that starts the multiline construct,) Tj T* (as in:) Tj T* () Tj T* (my_list = [) Tj T* (1, 2, 3,) Tj T* (4, 5, 6,) Tj T* (]) Tj T* (result = some_function_that_takes_arguments\() Tj T* ('a', 'b', 'c',) Tj T* ('d', 'e', 'f',) Tj T* (\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 3 of 27) Tj T* ET
endstream
