BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* (declaration.) Tj T* () Tj T* (In the standard library, non-UTF-8 encodings should be used only for test purposes. Use non-) Tj T* (ASCII characters sparingly, preferably only to denote places and human names. If using non-ASCII) Tj T* (characters as data, avoid noisy Unicode characters like z???a???l???g??o??? and byte order) Tj T* (marks.) Tj T* () Tj T* (All identifiers in the Python standard library MUST use ASCII-only identifiers, and SHOULD use) Tj T* (English words wherever feasible \(in many cases, abbreviations and technical terms are used which) Tj T* (aren't English\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (Open source projects with a global audience are encouraged to adopt a similar policy.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Imports) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Imports should usually be on separate lines:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* (import os) Tj T* (import sys) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong:) Tj T* (import sys, os) Tj T* () Tj T* (It's okay to say this though:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* (from subprocess import Popen, PIPE) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Imports are always put at the top of the file, just after any module) Tj T* (comments and docstrings, and before module globals and constants.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Imports should be grouped in the following order:) Tj T* () Tj T* (1. Standard library imports. 2. Related third party imports. 3. Local application/library) Tj T* (specific imports.) Tj T* () Tj T* (You should put a blank line between each group of imports.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Absolute imports are recommended, as they are usually more readable) Tj T* (and tend to be better behaved \(or at least give better error) Tj T* (messages\) if the import system is incorrectly configured \(such as) Tj T* (when a directory inside a package ends up on sys.path\):) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 6 of 27) Tj T* ET
endstream
