BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* (import mypkg.sibling) Tj T* (from mypkg import sibling) Tj T* (from mypkg.sibling import example) Tj T* () Tj T* (However, explicit relative imports are an acceptable alternative to absolute imports, especially) Tj T* (when dealing with complex package layouts where using absolute imports would be unnecessarily) Tj T* (verbose:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (from . import sibling) Tj T* (from .sibling import example) Tj T* () Tj T* (Standard library code should avoid complex package layouts and always use absolute imports.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- When importing a class from a class-containing module, it's usually) Tj T* (okay to spell this:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (from myclass import MyClass) Tj T* (from foo.bar.yourclass import YourClass) Tj T* () Tj T* (If this spelling causes local name clashes, then spell them explicitly:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (import myclass) Tj T* (import foo.bar.yourclass) Tj T* () Tj T* (and use myclass.MyClass and foo.bar.yourclass.YourClass.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Wildcard imports \(from <module> import *\) should be avoided, as) Tj T* (they make it unclear which names are present in the namespace,) Tj T* (confusing both readers and many automated tools. There is one) Tj T* (defensible use case for a wildcard import, which is to republish an) Tj T* (internal interface as part of a public API \(for example, overwriting) Tj T* (a pure Python implementation of an interface with the definitions) Tj T* (from an optional accelerator module and exactly which definitions) Tj T* (will be overwritten isn't known in advance\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (When republishing names this way, the guidelines below regarding public and internal interfaces) Tj T* (still apply.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Module Level Dunder Names) Tj T* () Tj T* (Module level "dunders" \(i.e. names with two leading and two trailing underscores\) such as) Tj T* (__all__, __author__, __version__, etc. should be placed after the module docstring but before) Tj T* (any import statements *except* from __future__ imports.  Python mandates that future-imports) Tj T* (must appear in the module before any other code except docstrings:) Tj T* () Tj T* ("""This is the example module.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 7 of 27) Tj T* ET
