BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (This module does stuff. """) Tj T* () Tj T* (from __future__ import barry_as_FLUFL) Tj T* () Tj T* (__all__ = ['a', 'b', 'c'] __version__ = '0.1' __author__ = 'Cardinal Biggles') Tj T* () Tj T* (import os import sys) Tj T* () Tj T* (String Quotes) Tj T* () Tj T* (In Python, single-quoted strings and double-quoted strings are the same.  This PEP does not make) Tj T* (a recommendation for this.  Pick a rule and stick to it.  When a string contains single or) Tj T* (double quote characters, however, use the other one to avoid backslashes in the string. It) Tj T* (improves readability.) Tj T* () Tj T* (For triple-quoted strings, always use double quote characters to be consistent with the) Tj T* (docstring convention in PEP 257.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Whitespace in Expressions and Statements) Tj T* () Tj T* (Pet Peeves) Tj T* () Tj T* (Avoid extraneous whitespace in the following situations:) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Immediately inside parentheses, brackets or braces:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* (spam\(ham[1], {eggs: 2}\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong:) Tj T* (spam\( ham[ 1 ], { eggs: 2 } \)) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Between a trailing comma and a following close parenthesis:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* (foo = \(0,\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong:) Tj T* (bar = \(0, \)) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Immediately before a comma, semicolon, or colon:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 8 of 27) Tj T* ET
