BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* (When to Use Trailing Commas) Tj T* () Tj T* (Trailing commas are usually optional, except they are mandatory when making a tuple of one) Tj T* (element.  For clarity, it is recommended to surround the latter in \(technically redundant\)) Tj T* (parentheses:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct: FILES = \('setup.cfg',\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong: FILES = 'setup.cfg',) Tj T* () Tj T* (When trailing commas are redundant, they are often helpful when a version control system is) Tj T* (used, when a list of values, arguments or imported items is expected to be extended over time.) Tj T* (The pattern is to put each value \(etc.\) on a line by itself, always adding a trailing comma, and) Tj T* (add the close parenthesis/bracket/brace on the next line. However it does not make sense to have) Tj T* (a trailing comma on the same line as the closing delimiter \(except in the above case of) Tj T* (singleton tuples\):) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* (FILES = [) Tj T* ('setup.cfg',) Tj T* ('tox.ini',) Tj T* (]) Tj T* (initialize\(FILES,) Tj T* (error=True,) Tj T* (\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong: FILES = ['setup.cfg', 'tox.ini',] initialize\(FILES, error=True,\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (Comments) Tj T* () Tj T* (Comments that contradict the code are worse than no comments.  Always make a priority of keeping) Tj T* (the comments up-to-date when the code changes!) Tj T* () Tj T* (Comments should be complete sentences.  The first word should be capitalized, unless it is an) Tj T* (identifier that begins with a lower case letter \(never alter the case of identifiers!\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (Block comments generally consist of one or more paragraphs built out of complete sentences, with) Tj T* (each sentence ending in a period.) Tj T* () Tj T* (You should use one or two spaces after a sentence-ending period in multi-sentence comments,) Tj T* (except after the final sentence.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Ensure that your comments are clear and easily understandable to other speakers of the language) Tj T* (you are writing in.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Python coders from non-English speaking countries: please write your comments in English, unless) Tj T* (you are 120% sure that the code will never be read by people who don't speak your language.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Block Comments) Tj T* () Tj T* (Block comments generally apply to some \(or all\) code that follows them, and are indented to the) Tj T* (same level as that code.  Each line of a block comment starts with a # and a single space) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 13 of 27) Tj T* ET
