BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* (implementations of Python \(PyPy, Jython, IronPython, Cython, Psyco,) Tj T* (and such\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (For example, do not rely on CPython's efficient implementation of in-place string concatenation) Tj T* (for statements in the form a += b or a = a + b.  This optimization is fragile even in CPython) Tj T* (\(it only works for some types\) and isn't present at all in implementations that don't use) Tj T* (refcounting.  In performance sensitive parts of the library, the ''.join\(\) form should be used) Tj T* (instead.  This will ensure that concatenation occurs in linear time across various) Tj T* (implementations.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Comparisons to singletons like None should always be done with) Tj T* (is or is not, never the equality operators.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Also, beware of writing if x when you really mean if x is not None -- e.g. when testing whether) Tj T* (a variable or argument that defaults to None was set to some other value.  The other value might) Tj T* (have a type \(such as a container\) that could be false in a boolean context!) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Use is not operator rather than not ... is.  While both) Tj T* (expressions are functionally identical, the former is more readable) Tj T* (and preferred:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* (if foo is not None:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong:) Tj T* (if not foo is None:) Tj T* () Tj T* (- When implementing ordering operations with rich comparisons, it is) Tj T* (best to implement all six operations \(__eq__, __ne__,) Tj T* (__lt__, __le__, __gt__, __ge__\) rather than relying) Tj T* (on other code to only exercise a particular comparison.) Tj T* () Tj T* (To minimize the effort involved, the functools.total_ordering\(\) decorator provides a tool to) Tj T* (generate missing comparison methods.) Tj T* () Tj T* (PEP 207 indicates that reflexivity rules *are* assumed by Python. Thus, the interpreter may swap) Tj T* (y > x with x < y, y >= x with x <= y, and may swap the arguments of x == y and x != y.  The) Tj T* (sort\(\) and min\(\) operations are guaranteed to use the < operator and the max\(\) function uses the) Tj T* (> operator.  However, it is best to implement all six operations so that confusion doesn't arise) Tj T* (in other contexts.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Always use a def statement instead of an assignment statement that binds) Tj T* (a lambda expression directly to an identifier:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* (def f\(x\): return 2*x) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 20 of 27) Tj T* ET
endstream
