BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong:) Tj T* (f = lambda x: 2*x) Tj T* () Tj T* (The first form means that the name of the resulting function object is specifically 'f' instead) Tj T* (of the generic '<lambda>'. This is more useful for tracebacks and string representations in) Tj T* (general. The use of the assignment statement eliminates the sole benefit a lambda expression can) Tj T* (offer over an explicit def statement \(i.e. that it can be embedded inside a larger expression\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Derive exceptions from Exception rather than BaseException.) Tj T* (Direct inheritance from BaseException is reserved for exceptions) Tj T* (where catching them is almost always the wrong thing to do.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Design exception hierarchies based on the distinctions that code) Tj T* (*catching* the exceptions is likely to need, rather than the locations) Tj T* (where the exceptions are raised. Aim to answer the question) Tj T* ("What went wrong?" programmatically, rather than only stating that) Tj T* ("A problem occurred" \(see PEP 3151 for an example of this lesson being) Tj T* (learned for the builtin exception hierarchy\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (Class naming conventions apply here, although you should add the suffix "Error" to your) Tj T* (exception classes if the exception is an error.  Non-error exceptions that are used for non-) Tj T* (local flow control or other forms of signaling need no special suffix.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Use exception chaining appropriately. raise X from Y) Tj T* (should be used to indicate explicit replacement without losing the) Tj T* (original traceback.) Tj T* () Tj T* (When deliberately replacing an inner exception \(using raise X from None\), ensure that relevant) Tj T* (details are transferred to the new exception \(such as preserving the attribute name when) Tj T* (converting KeyError to AttributeError, or embedding the text of the original exception in the) Tj T* (new exception message\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (- When catching exceptions, mention specific exceptions whenever) Tj T* (possible instead of using a bare except: clause:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (try:) Tj T* (import platform_specific_module) Tj T* (except ImportError:) Tj T* (platform_specific_module = None) Tj T* () Tj T* (A bare except: clause will catch SystemExit and KeyboardInterrupt exceptions, making it harder) Tj T* (to interrupt a program with Control-C, and can disguise other problems.  If you want to catch) Tj T* (all exceptions that signal program errors, use except Exception: \(bare except is equivalent to) Tj T* (except BaseException:\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (A good rule of thumb is to limit use of bare 'except' clauses to two cases:) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 21 of 27) Tj T* ET
endstream
