BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* (1. If the exception handler will be printing out or logging the) Tj T* (traceback; at least the user will be aware that an error has) Tj T* (occurred.) Tj T* () Tj T* (2. If the code needs to do some cleanup work, but then lets the) Tj T* (exception propagate upwards with raise.  try...finally) Tj T* (can be a better way to handle this case.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- When catching operating system errors, prefer the explicit exception) Tj T* (hierarchy introduced in Python 3.3 over introspection of errno) Tj T* (values.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Additionally, for all try/except clauses, limit the try clause) Tj T* (to the absolute minimum amount of code necessary.  Again, this) Tj T* (avoids masking bugs:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* (try:) Tj T* (value = collection[key]) Tj T* (except KeyError:) Tj T* (return key_not_found\(key\)) Tj T* (else:) Tj T* (return handle_value\(value\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong:) Tj T* (try:) Tj T* (# Too broad!) Tj T* (return handle_value\(collection[key]\)) Tj T* (except KeyError:) Tj T* (# Will also catch KeyError raised by handle_value\(\)) Tj T* (return key_not_found\(key\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (- When a resource is local to a particular section of code, use a) Tj T* (with statement to ensure it is cleaned up promptly and reliably) Tj T* (after use. A try/finally statement is also acceptable.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Context managers should be invoked through separate functions or methods) Tj T* (whenever they do something other than acquire and release resources:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* (with conn.begin_transaction\(\):) Tj T* (do_stuff_in_transaction\(conn\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong:) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 22 of 27) Tj T* ET
endstream
