BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* (with conn:) Tj T* (do_stuff_in_transaction\(conn\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (The latter example doesn't provide any information to indicate that the __enter__ and __exit__) Tj T* (methods are doing something other than closing the connection after a transaction.  Being) Tj T* (explicit is important in this case.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Be consistent in return statements.  Either all return statements in) Tj T* (a function should return an expression, or none of them should.  If) Tj T* (any return statement returns an expression, any return statements) Tj T* (where no value is returned should explicitly state this as return) Tj T* (None, and an explicit return statement should be present at the) Tj T* (end of the function \(if reachable\):) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* () Tj T* (def foo\(x\):) Tj T* (if x >= 0:) Tj T* (return math.sqrt\(x\)) Tj T* (else:) Tj T* (return None) Tj T* () Tj T* (def bar\(x\):) Tj T* (if x < 0:) Tj T* (return None) Tj T* (return math.sqrt\(x\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong:) Tj T* () Tj T* (def foo\(x\):) Tj T* (if x >= 0:) Tj T* (return math.sqrt\(x\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (def bar\(x\):) Tj T* (if x < 0:) Tj T* (return) Tj T* (return math.sqrt\(x\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Use ''.startswith\(\) and ''.endswith\(\) instead of string) Tj T* (slicing to check for prefixes or suffixes.) Tj T* () Tj T* (startswith\(\) and endswith\(\) are cleaner and less error prone:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* (if foo.startswith\('bar'\):) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 23 of 27) Tj T* ET
endstream
