BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (PEP 8 Style Guide for Python Code) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (- Users who don't want to use type checkers are free to ignore them.) Tj T* (However, it is expected that users of third party library packages) Tj T* (may want to run type checkers over those packages.  For this purpose) Tj T* (PEP 484 recommends the use of stub files: .pyi files that are read) Tj T* (by the type checker in preference of the corresponding .py files.) Tj T* (Stub files can be distributed with a library, or separately \(with) Tj T* (the library author's permission\) through the typeshed repo [5].) Tj T* () Tj T* (Variable Annotations) Tj T* () Tj T* (PEP 526 introduced variable annotations. The style recommendations for them are similar to those) Tj T* (on function annotations described above:) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Annotations for module level variables, class and instance variables,) Tj T* (and local variables should have a single space after the colon.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- There should be no space before the colon.) Tj T* () Tj T* (- If an assignment has a right hand side, then the equality sign should have) Tj T* (exactly one space on both sides:) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Correct:) Tj T* () Tj T* (code: int) Tj T* () Tj T* (class Point:) Tj T* (coords: Tuple[int, int]) Tj T* (label: str = '<unknown>') Tj T* () Tj T* (.. code-block:) Tj T* () Tj T* (# Wrong:) Tj T* () Tj T* (code:int  # No space after colon) Tj T* (code : int  # Space before colon) Tj T* () Tj T* (class Test:) Tj T* (result: int=0  # No spaces around equality sign) Tj T* () Tj T* (- Although the PEP 526 is accepted for Python 3.6, the variable annotation) Tj T* (syntax is the preferred syntax for stub files on all versions of Python) Tj T* (\(see PEP 484 for details\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (.. [#fn-hi] *Hanging indentation* is a type-setting style where all the lines in a paragraph are) Tj T* (indented except the first line.  In the context of Python, the term is used to describe a style) Tj T* (where the opening parenthesis of a parenthesized statement is the last non-whitespace character) Tj T* (of the line, with subsequent lines being indented until the closing parenthesis.) Tj T* () Tj T* (References) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 26 of 27) Tj T* ET
endstream
